  "limits": [
    "Clinical deletion covers the complete connected protected three-tool store, not an individual student or every application store. Logical replacement is not forensic disk erasure.",
    "Old noncooperating app windows, encrypted backups, exports, general recovery, browser caches and external provider copies require separate disposition. Explicit backup restore can restore previously deleted records.",
    "Known retention/hold conventions and operator acknowledgments are not a complete legal-hold detector or district staff identity system.",
    "Owned-Firestore tooling targets one expired assignment with an existing owner-matching parent. It does not administer Google-provisioned Canvas storage or infer ownership for previously orphaned sessions.",
    "Actual writers must be stopped. Transactions bind parent changes/holds to each delete, but arbitrary new child creation or future writes cannot be excluded by enumeration alone. Partial/unknown results are not success.",
    "Plan files contain exact resource paths, UIDs and approval references; protect them as administrative records. Receipts avoid record bodies but identifiers can still be sensitive.",
    "Mailbox v26 source must be redeployed; cache access expiry is not a scheduled physical purge. Drive trash, permanent deletion, submissions, delivered files, Vault and recipients are distinct outcomes.",
    "Offline receipt review validates operator observations only and always reports providerPurgeVerified:false and allCopiesDeleted:false.",
    "The district must approve record schedules, holds, service/account scope, deletion authority and actual deployment. No live operator cleanup or full coordinated release has occurred."
  ]
